Feature	Native App	Hybrid App	Web App
Definition	Developed specifically for a mobile operating system.	Combines web technologies with a native app container.	Runs in a mobile web browser.
Technology	Java/Kotlin for Android, Swift for iOS.	HTML, CSS, JavaScript with native components.	HTML, CSS, JavaScript.
Installation	Installed from an app store.	Usually installed from an app store.	Opened through a browser; usually no installation required.
Performance	Generally fast and responsive.	Depends on the implementation and web content.	Depends on the browser and website.
Device Features	Can access camera, GPS, and other device features.	Can access device features through native APIs or plugins.	Access is limited by browser support and permissions.
Internet	Some features can work offline.	Some features can work offline.	Usually requires internet, depending on the website.
Example	Instagram mobile app.	An app built using Ionic with embedded web content.	Flipkart website opened in Chrome.
